  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the second of six runs: all 7 witnesses gave their planned verdicts.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_484B_560_7a.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** `x` must be a vehicle under the aggregate `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **When it applies:** there is a railway crossing `r` that `x` is entering, or has entered and has stayed within 15 ft of since. The 15 ft is the text's own figure, written as `Units.feet 15`.\n- **The duty:** `x` is not halted, judged against `p.speed_resolution`. A halt is excused only when a police officer's direction to stop governs a travel region `x` is on.\n\n**Gate runs:**\n1. `UNUSED_CLAIM` for `drv.motion.entering_region`. The clearance concept already checks for the entry internally, but the gate wants every claimed concept named in the rule itself. I added the entry as an \"or\" alongside the clearance check. Under the clearance concept's contract an entry already makes the clearance check true, so this changes no verdict at any observation.\n2. OK.\n\nI added no narrowings; the record's own covered everything.\n\n**Witnesses:** a 6 m crossing on a roadway and a 4.5 m car. Every trace starts well short of the crossing, so the first observation already shows the car hasn't entered it.\n\n| Scenario | What happens | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | halts on the crossing, truck queued beyond | violated |\n| permit | crosses steadily, halts with its rear end 16.75 m past | compliant |\n| idle | no crossing; halts at a stop line | not applicable |\n| blind | as forbid, with speed unobserved | unknown |\n| branch_1 | halts with its rear end 2 m past (under 15 ft, which is 4.572 m) | violated |\n| branch_2 | halts on the crossing while a police officer directs it to stop | compliant |\n| branch_3 | crosses alone, halts with its rear end 6 m past | compliant |\n\nThe run log is in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
